//? Title: Dilated Convolution: Expanded Kernels and Sampling Gaps
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Image features need distant context without reducing their spatial resolution. Dilated
convolution spaces filter taps apart. We compare its tensor forward and backward maps with
zero-expanded kernels, visualise the sampled support, and train two equal-size predictors
whose access to the target's context differs.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.1_fundamentals/dilated_convolutions.cpp`.

> The method

A length-k kernel at dilation d spans k_eff=1+d(k-1) sites but still stores k taps.
Replacing each gap with constant zeros gives the same linear map and gradients in the original
taps. Spatial padding must use the effective kernel. In two dimensions the multiply count is
unchanged at fixed output dimensions, while the sampled positions change.

$$
r_L=1+2\sum_{l=1}^L d_l\quad(k_l=3,s_l=1),\qquad
\operatorname{supp}(\partial y_0/\partial x)=
\left\{\sum_l d_l u_l:u_l\in\{-1,0,1\}\right\}.
$$
\alttext(Three-tap layers enlarge the enclosing receptive width by twice each dilation; actual support consists of sums of the sampled offsets.)

An enclosing box need not be densely sampled. Rates (2,2,2) reach only even offsets;
(1,2,4) fill every integer offset from -7 to 7. Tensor input gradients expose the actual
support rather than just its enclosing width. The native path avoids materialising zero
weights; the expanded filter is an independent reference, not an acceleration.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/dilated_convolutions_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/dilated_convolutions_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/dilated_convolutions_concept.tikz > build/dilated_convolutions_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/dilated_convolutions_concept.svg build/dilated_convolutions_concept.dvi > build/dilated_convolutions_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
